    <!-- column headers -->
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="160" width="380" height="22">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="11" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(100,116,139,1)" bold="true" wrap="false"><p>LIMITATION</p></content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="470" topLeftY="160" width="434" height="22">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="11" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(34,211,238,1)" bold="true" wrap="false"><p>HOW WE HANDLE IT</p></content>
    </shape>
    <line startX="56" startY="188" endX="904" endY="188"><border color="rgba(148,163,184,0.25)" width="1"/></line>

    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="204" width="380" height="22">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(241,245,249,1)" wrap="false"><p>Forecasts are probabilities, not certainties</p></content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="470" topLeftY="204" width="434" height="22">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(148,163,184,1)" wrap="false"><p>We show P10–P90 bands and calibrate them; true black swans stay open.</p></content>
    </shape>
    <line startX="56" startY="238" endX="904" endY="238"><border color="rgba(148,163,184,0.12)" width="1"/></line>

    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="252" width="380" height="22">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(241,245,249,1)" wrap="false"><p>Output depends on the quality of the world spec</p></content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="470" topLeftY="252" width="434" height="22">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(148,163,184,1)" wrap="false"><p>Typed specs and deterministic simulation keep inputs honest.</p></content>
    </shape>
    <line startX="56" startY="286" endX="904" endY="286"><border color="rgba(148,163,184,0.12)" width="1"/></line>

    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="300" width="380" height="22">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(241,245,249,1)" wrap="false"><p>Calibration needs a large historical case library</p></content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="470" topLeftY="300" width="434" height="22">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(148,163,184,1)" wrap="false"><p>We expand it continuously and disclose the nearest-case distance.</p></content>
    </shape>
    <line startX="56" startY="334" endX="904" endY="334"><border color="rgba(148,163,184,0.12)" width="1"/></line>

    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="348" width="380" height="22">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(241,245,249,1)" wrap="false"><p>Generation can still fail on edge cases</p></content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="470" topLeftY="348" width="434" height="22">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(148,163,184,1)" wrap="false"><p>Gates plus a template fallback; a human reviews before release.</p></content>
    </shape>

    <line startX="56" startY="400" endX="904" endY="400"><border color="rgba(34,211,238,0.3)" width="1"/></line>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="420" width="848" height="28">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="14" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(241,245,249,1)" bold="true" wrap="false">
        <p>This is decision support. We make the trade-offs visible; the human still decides.</p>
      </content>
    </shape>

    <line startX="56" startY="496" endX="904" endY="496"><border color="rgba(148,163,184,0.15)" width="1"/></line>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="504" width="500" height="18">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="10" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(100,116,139,1)" wrap="false"><p>OpenGame  ·  Investor Briefing</p></content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="820" topLeftY="504" width="84" height="18">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="10" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(100,116,139,1)" textAlign="right" wrap="false"><p>19 / 20</p></content>
    </shape>
  </data>
  <note>
    <content textType="body" fontSize="14" fontFamily="Inter">
      <p>We want to be candid about what the system is and is not. It outputs probabilities, not certainties, and a genuinely unprecedented event cannot be forecast; we show the bands and keep the tails open. The quality of a prediction depends on the quality of the world spec, which is why specs are typed and the simulator is deterministic. Calibration is only as good as the case library, and we are growing it while disclosing how close the nearest case is. On edge cases, generation can still fail, so gates and a template fallback protect the output and a human reviews. The system is a decision aid that makes trade-offs visible, not a replacement for judgment. We believe this honesty is itself a reason to trust the numbers.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
